<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- Corner radius of the widget as the user places it: the Glance runtime background
         (TaskWidgetDesign) and the static android:initialLayout backgrounds.

         This is the app's own design value and is deliberately NOT pinned to the platform's
         enforced radius. On a host that clips (see below) a value rounder than the clip is what
         the widget's silhouette actually becomes, because our fill then sits wholly inside the
         clip; on API 26-30, where nothing clips, it is the silhouette outright. Lowering it is a
         visible change to every placed widget on every home screen, so change it as a design
         decision with a device in hand, not as a side effect of a picker fix. -->
    <dimen name="tday_widget_surface_corner_radius">24dp</dimen>

    <!-- Corner radius of the widget-picker preview art (widget_preview_bg_today/floater), which
         is a different surface from the one above: it only ever renders inside the launcher's
         widget picker, on API 31+ (previewLayout) and API 35+ (setWidgetPreview).

         This one MUST NOT be larger than the radius the host clips the preview to. Since
         Android 12 the picker clips the preview card to its own enforced radius
         (`android:dimen/system_app_widget_background_radius`, capped by Launcher3's
         `enforced_rounded_corner_max_radius`). A rounder-than-the-clip background does not look
         rounder — our fill lands entirely inside the clip, and the crescent between the two arcs
         is a hole in our own artwork. The picker paints an opaque light surface behind the card,
         so the hole reads as a thin light outline around it. That is the bug this value fixes.

         16dp is the AOSP default of both platform values above, so the art stays at or inside the
         clip on any launcher. Do not raise it above PLATFORM_ENFORCED_RADIUS_DP in
         WidgetCornerRadiusTest. -->
    <dimen name="tday_widget_picker_preview_corner_radius">16dp</dimen>
</resources>
